{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Parts on the Garage Floor.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Parts on the Garage Floor.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"parts on the garage floor parts on the garage floor","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Parts on the Garage Floor.md","fileName":"Parts on the Garage Floor.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Parts on the Garage Floor","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 15:58\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Design Methods]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Design Methods","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Parts on the Garage Floor.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Parts on the Garage Floor.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"parts on the garage floor parts on the garage floor","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Parts on the Garage Floor.md","fileName":"Parts on the Garage Floor.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Parts on the Garage Floor","heading":"Parts on the Garage Floor","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Parts on the Garage Floor is a development dysfunction in which disciplines polish separate components across many iterations but postpone assembling a playable whole. Local task progress hides uncertainty about integration and the actual experience.\n\nThe remedy is to select thinner slices that combine design, code, art, audio, and testing into playable value each Sprint. Integration then becomes a source of continuing knowledge rather than an end-stage crisis.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Design Methods","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Parts on the Garage Floor.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Parts on the Garage Floor.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearch